 a prime number.\n\n can be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\n¬P∨Q.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28cb0c9e-bf5a-5cab-9147-77e827e21bb2" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Conjunction Using De Morgan's Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b23503c3-c0f4-55cb-866a-a03351a4b2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "and" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414597} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c1d23c-ef3f-5c69-86f0-b7c9d0d1b96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "or" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c1d23c-ef3f-5c69-86f0-b7c9d0d1b96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "or" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414598} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf06d45-98ed-5085-96df-bd18bfa04150" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7998afd3-52dc-5747-a7d8-358bbbfe48ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$m$ is even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414584} {:answer/id #uuid "f5cd876b-13b1-5225-b821-138febd1907c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$m$ is odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5cd876b-13b1-5225-b821-138febd1907c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$m$ is odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414612} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c9ea37c-bf39-5b29-b153-16db33fc5e4e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414618} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75c9ac14-9d05-5645-bb43-64477de4c933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$n$ is prime" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414583} {:answer/id #uuid "afd3d5be-9813-598c-9630-53282446c9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$n$ is not prime" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afd3d5be-9813-598c-9630-53282446c9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$n$ is not prime" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414595} :answer-field/id #uuid "c20a8900-7338-538f-8233-6d86f1813173" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "501a9cd9-7487-5eca-998b-73598c18e09d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183284" :question/problem "$\\,$ $n$  is prime and  $m$  is even.\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∧B)=¬A∨¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$n$ is prime and $m$ is even\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(n\\text{ is prime and }m\\text{ is even}) & ≡¬(n\\text{ is prime}∧m\\text{ is even}) \\\\  & ≡¬(n\\text{ is prime})∨¬(m\\text{ is even}) \\\\  & ≡n\\text{ is not prime}∨m\\text{ is odd} \\\\  & ≡n\\text{ is not prime or }m\\text{ is odd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198257 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28cb0c9e-bf5a-5cab-9147-77e827e21bb2" :knowledge-point/title "Negating a Conjunction Using De Morgan's Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b44f959-eafb-5fb0-8cf3-b67b16dc0e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186