0be-c520-5735-8b0d-89789f1b6296" :question/math-academy-id "q-183310" :question/problem "$\\,$ $a\\le -1\\text{ or }b=0.$ \n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:" :question/worked-solution "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$a\\le -1\\text{ or }b=0$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(a\\le -1\\text{ or }b=0) & ≡¬(a\\le -1∨b=0) \\\\  & ≡¬(a\\le -1)∧¬(b=0) \\\\  & ≡a>-1∧b\\ne 0 \\\\  & ≡a>-1\\text{ and }b\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
